package server

const mcpProcessHierarchyPolicy = " Hierarchical processes are first-class semantic scopes: model.processes contains id,name,description?,parentId?; nodes[].processId assigns direct membership. SchemaVersion 1 remains backward compatible when processes is omitted. Discover hierarchical-processes/process-drilldown through capabilities.hierarchy, read GET .../simulation/hierarchy for rootProcessIds and process records with childProcessIds,nodeIds,directNodeIds, and use versioned processes CRUD. GET .../runs/{runId}/processes or /processes/{entityId} exposes actual scoped metrics and /queues includes processes. Scopes use the same global engine and shared-resource pools; folded cards add no processing time, capacity or costs. completed counts successful scope visits, exited counts successful boundary exits, and terminalCompleted counts successful final outcomes within the scope. cycleTime is scope-entry-to-exit/outcome and scoped ttr is scope-entry-to-revenue-producing terminal outcome. Parent and child rollups overlap: do not sum them or node quantiles. Only occupied shared-resource cost is allocated to scopes; idle/scaling/investment pool overhead remains global. Referenced process deletions return structured 422; use complete model PUT to reassign nodes/reparent children atomically. GET /templates also discovers the Delivery network example with nested subprocesses, shared global resources and bottleneck-migration scenarios; POST /diagrams retains the kiosk default."
